// ONCO-ASCAT-001 — shared inputs and R expectations of the Battenberg callSubclones tests (B24 F60/F61).
// Evidence: docs/Evidence/ONCO-ASCAT-001-Evidence.md (§ F60, § F61); TestSpec: tests/TestSpecs/ONCO-ASCAT-001.md (§19, §20).
// Source: Wedge-lab/battenberg master (57a8f7e) R/fitcopynumber.R (callSubclones, determine_copynumber, merge_segments,
//         mask_high_cn_segments), R/orderEdges.R; GenomicRanges 1.54.1 / GenomeInfoDb (makeGRangesFromDataFrame seqlevels).
//
// Genomes are generated in-test by the integer LCG x ← (1664525·x + 1013904223) mod 2^24, u = x / 2^24 (exact in IEEE
// double in R and C#), block by block: per SNP i = 1..n at pos0 + i·step, BAFphased = clamp(baf + bsd·(u₁ + u₂ + u₃ − 1.5)·2)
// (= BAF), BAFseg = the block's seg value, a logR probe at the same position lr + lsd·(u₁ + u₂ + u₃ − 1.5)·2 (NA every
// naEvery-th SNP). Expected values: the Battenberg functions sourced verbatim in R 4.3.3 (GenomicRanges 1.54.1) running
// callSubclones' sequence set.seed(rseed); determine_copynumber; merge_segments; determine_copynumber;
// mask_high_cn_segments (gamma 1, siglevel 0.05, maxdist 0.01, noperms 1000, cn_upper_limit 1000), printed with %.17g.
// Row arrays: BAF, pval, LogR, ntot, then nMaj1, nMin1, frac1, nMaj2, nMin2, frac2, SDfrac, SDfrac_BS, frac1_0.025,
// frac1_0.975 for solutions A–F (NA = NaN).

